      "intro": "If your loved one struggles with heating bills in Connecticut, CEAP can provide $295-$645 toward their energy costs this winter. Because the program pays utility companies directly, your loved one won't handle cash, the assistance goes straight toward their heating bill, electric bill, or fuel delivery. Households with elderly members, disabled individuals, or children under 6 receive higher benefit amounts.\n\nThe program runs from September 1, 2025 through May 29, 2026, but funds are limited and distributed first-come, first-served. Because crisis assistance is available for households facing fuel emergencies, eligible families can get fuel delivery authorization within 18 hours if they're running out of heating oil or propane.\n\nIncome limit: $47,764/year for a single person, $62,460 for a couple (2025-2026). No asset test this year. If your loved one receives SNAP, SSI, or TANF, they automatically qualify regardless of other income.",
